{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 134, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free skip on edge 0 with a conv gains much more (rows 3 and 6) than replacing a conv or none."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing skip on edge 5 with a 3x3 conv gives the largest gains (row 53 and row 56) compared with replacing convs (rows 57 and 60)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping pooling for a conv on the output edge gives a big gain in pool-heavy parents (rows 54 and 58)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on edge 0 consistently hurts on all three datasets (rows 71, 75, 79 and 80)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a skip on edge 0 helps or is neutral (rows 73 and 76), unlike removing a conv, which hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the direct input-to-output 3x3 conv costs accuracy on all three datasets (rows 61 and 68), most of all on ImageNet16."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on edge 4 with a 3x3 conv gives big gains in pool-heavy parents (row 44) and small positive gains elsewhere (row 47)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on edge 2 with a 1x1 conv helps on all three datasets (rows 94 and 96), more than replacing a conv (rows 91 and 95)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3"